Make PairCaloCLustersPi0 more efficient.

PairCaloClustersPi0 tries to find all pairs of clusters with invariant mass
consistent with the pi0 mass, subject to the constraint that no cluster
is used by more than one pair.  It was doing this combinatoric problem
by exhaustive search, which was exponential in both space and time.
As a result, it was basically impossible to use the algorithm on
hadronic events, as it would gobble up all available virtual memory.

The combinatoric problem is, however, equivalent to that of finding
a maximum matching of a graph (<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matching_(graph_theory)>).
Boost.graph supplies an algorithm (Galil, https://doi.org/10.1145/6462.6502)
that solves this in N^3 time (and i think linear space).
Rewrite this algorithm to use this.

(A N^2 logN algorithm is known but not implemented in boost.graph.
As the one from boost is fast enough that this algorithms is no longer
a bottleneck in hadronic events, just use that.)